---
// Plain-language "who/what" statement placed right under the hero, kept as
// real visible text on purpose: the hero headline is a slogan, and search
// engines / AI answer engines lift a short, self-contained answer far more
// reliably than they infer one from marketing copy. Keep it ~30-60 words and
// in sync with the Person schema in BaseLayout.astro and public/llms.txt.
---

<section id="intro" class="intro" aria-label="About Doug Rosenberg in brief">
  <div class="wrap intro__grid">
    <p class="intro__text">
      <strong>Doug Rosenberg</strong> is a Chicago-based jazz saxophonist, composer, and educator,
      with the debut album <em>Better Than TV</em> (2014), a New England Conservatory degree, and
      performances at Millennium Park, the Green Mill, and Symphony Center. He also designs and
      builds websites for musicians and small businesses.
    </p>
    {/* Facts rail (2026-11-15): the same facts as the paragraph, as ruled rows
         like the On record ledger. The paragraph stays as the visible,
         lift-able answer for search; this is a second view of it, so keep the
         two in sync. */}
    <dl class="intro__facts">
      <div class="intro__fact"><dt>Debut</dt><dd><em>Better Than TV</em>, 2014</dd></div>
      <div class="intro__fact"><dt>Degree</dt><dd>New England Conservatory</dd></div>
      <div class="intro__fact"><dt>Stages</dt><dd>Millennium Park &middot; Green Mill &middot; Symphony Center</dd></div>
      <div class="intro__fact"><dt>Also</dt><dd>Websites for musicians and small businesses</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    background: transparent;
  }

  /* Left-aligned on the same edge as every section heading below it, and
     set as a lede (2026-10-25): centered, it was the one section breaking
     the page's left axis. */
  .intro__text {
    /* Larger than the 44rem / 1.4rem it had (2026-11-01). It still left the
       right 40% empty at 56rem, so from 900px the facts rail takes that side
       (2026-11-15). Below 900px it is one column and the rail sits under it. */
    max-width: 56rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.8vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .intro__text strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .intro__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .intro__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
      align-items: start;
    }

    /* A smaller lede beside the rail so it wraps to about eight lines, not
       ten: the prototype's 1.6rem balanced the two columns. */
    .intro__text {
      font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 1.9vw, 1.6rem);
    }
  }

  .intro__facts {
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--staff-line-strong);
  }

  .intro__fact {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--staff-line-strong);
  }

  .intro__fact dt {
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .intro__fact dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
